M9 file workspace:
- The file tree symbols are from @pierre/trees 1.0.0-beta.6, Apache-2.0,
  commit 548416a7ec3ff3ff553636af60a31d1b21eca873. The unmodified sprite,
  source manifest and upstream notices are copied from the reviewed prototype.
  See licenses/M9-tree-icons/ for the license and provenance.
- CodeMirror, Markdown, math/diagram and PDF engines and their installed runtime
  dependencies are recorded in licenses/M9/manifest.json with upstream notices.
- Text conflict inline diff reuses @codemirror/merge 6.12.1 (MIT), with its
  original license and dependencies retained in licenses/M9/. Its decorations
  never choose the persisted file version; the workspace owns those decisions.
- The dollar-math token matcher in src/shared/markdown-dollar-math.mjs adapts
  markdown-it-texmath 1.0.0 (Stefan Goessner, MIT) without its eager CJS engine
  dependency. Its full license is retained in
  licenses/M9/markdown-it-texmath@1.0.0__license.txt.txt.
- The production PDF text-layer styling adapts pdfjs-dist 5.4.296 (Apache-2.0).
- Notebook HTML and SVG parsing uses parse5 8.0.1 (MIT) and saxes 6.0.0 (ISC), with
  entities/xmlchars dependencies; licenses and hashes are in licenses/M9/.
  Its CMaps, standard fonts and image decoder assets are bundled unchanged under
  out/renderer/pdf-assets, including their embedded licenses and notices.
- CSV/TSV field decoding uses Papa Parse 5.5.3 (MIT); its upstream license is
  retained in licenses/M9/. Source editing does not serialize through the parser.
- HTML document resource discovery uses parse5-sax-parser 8.0.0, PostCSS 8.5.30,
  postcss-value-parser 4.2.0 and es-module-lexer 2.3.2 (MIT), without evaluating
  project scripts. Upstream notices and dependency hashes are in licenses/M9/.
- TeX compilation uses Tectonic 0.17.0 and the pinned WillYou TeX v33 resource
  selection. Original resources are unchanged; selection and ZIP packaging are
  WillYou's work. The engine, original source archive, font/macro notices and
  per-file provenance accompany the offline bundle in native/tex/licenses/.
  This collection has multiple licenses; it is not uniformly MIT.
- pdf-lib 1.17.1 (MIT) is used in an isolated worker solely to add an empty content
  stream to blank PDF image pages in private TeX snapshots. Original project
  files are not rewritten. Its runtime notices are retained in licenses/M9/.
- Office ZIP processing uses yauzl 3.4.0 (MIT) and yazl 3.3.1 (MIT); their notices
  and dependency hashes are retained in licenses/M9/. Calculation uses the fixed
  Eclipse Temurin JRE 21.0.12.1+1 and Apache POI 5.5.1 with its 13 dependency JARs.
  Original JRE legal texts accompany native/office/jre/legal; POI notices, POMs,
  source URLs and checksums accompany native/office/licenses. These components
  retain their respective licenses. The WillYou Java helper is project code.
  Eclipse ECJ 3.43.0 is a build-only compiler and is not shipped in the runtime.
- Spreadsheet display number formats use SheetJS SSF 0.11.2 (Apache-2.0).
  Original cell storage is retained; the formatter is not a workbook writer or
  formula evaluator. Its upstream notice is retained in licenses/M9/.
- DOCX/PPTX layout uses the complete, unmodified LibreOffice 26.2.4.2 bundle
  (build 0229ac93fcf0d7cbc6376066c6f35021cef002dc), retaining its vendor signatures,
  component licenses and notices in native/libreoffice/LibreOffice.app/Contents/Resources/.
  The official download URLs and per-file checksums accompany resources.json.
  LibreOffice and its components retain their respective licenses, including
  MPL-2.0; corresponding source is available at
  https://downloadarchive.documentfoundation.org/libreoffice/old/26.2.4.2/src/.
  WillYou's private-profile rendering boundary is project code. No LibreOffice
  source or binary is modified, and rendered PDFs do not replace source files.
- File identity/authorization, native macOS save/recovery broker, source/EOL
  mapping and production state/lifecycle code are WillYou implementations.
  They reuse this repository's reviewed M9 prototype and P1 experiments.
  No private Codex implementation, font or toolbar icon is distributed.

- Code syntax highlighting uses Shiki 3.20.0 (MIT) with its public JavaScript
  regex engine and unmodified TextMate grammars from tm-grammars 1.26.0. Individual
  grammars retain their respective upstream licenses; the complete pinned
  grammar NOTICE and dependency licenses are in licenses/M9/code-highlighting/.
  Shared code, Markdown and Notebook token colors adapt @pierre/theme 2.0.0
  (Apache-2.0, including its retained Primer MIT notice): three decorator rules
  are omitted and the remaining palette is independently adjusted to observed
  reference color facts. No private Codex code or grammar asset is distributed.

